  "releaseNotes": "FastEqualityComparer and FastComparer no longer reach the default comparer through reflection. Each comparison allocated a two-element argument array and boxed its result, costing sixty-four bytes and about fourteen nanoseconds; a comparison is now a virtual call and two unboxes, costing about four tenths of a nanosecond and nothing. The types and their members are unchanged, so consumers need do nothing to receive this.",
